\par\par \b \uc2  Wall Street supports some  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil FX intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Apu Sikri \par \uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1999\par 21:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Oct 26 (Reuters) - Wall Street analysts and international investors Wednesday voiced support for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying a stable real is key to containing inflationary expectations and holding down interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The Latin American country, operating in relatively illiquid markets, needs the flexibility to avoid any sharp declines in the real, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "These can be fairly illiquid markets which can result in sharp moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Paulo Leme, managing director of emerging markets research at Goldman Sachs & Co. \par \par \uc2  "With a temporary deterioration in cash flows, having scope for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the smart thing to do," Leme said, adding that he sees the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as undervalued by 25 percent on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday, driving the real to 1.992 to the dollar from the day's weak point of 2.004. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later confirmed that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced earlier this week it will seek to renegotiate minimum \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve requirements with the International Monetary Fund, to have more reserves at its disposal for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  "needs to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because a weaker real has an adverse impact on the budget though the debt structure and secondly, it restrains the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from reducing interest rates," said Mohamed El-Erian, portfolio manager at the Pacific Investment Management Co. (PIMCO). \par \par \uc2  "Even in a flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, they just can't let the real go," said Jose Barrionuevo, head of sovereign bond research at Lehman Brothers. "It would have too much of an impact on interest rates and the fiscal side," he said. \par \par \uc2  A weaker real would ignite inflationary pressures and limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to lower interest rates and trim the government's expenditure on interest payments. \par \par \uc2  Supporters of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy are quick to add that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to support the real only on the margins and abstain from any large-scale use of reserves. \par \par \uc2  "When a country needs to revert a big current account deficit like the $25 billion that Brazil has and there is no funding for it from external sources, then there is a school of thought that says that during the transition, you should support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader at a large European bank. \par \par \uc2  "It's worth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  until exports pick up owing to the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it is still a bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking," said the trader. \par \par \uc2  Investors pointed out that Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga, who came to the bank from the hedge fund Soros Fund Management LP, strongly believes in free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has indicated he supports \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in limited measure to smooth out any sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. \par \par \uc2  Brazil let the real float in January after spending billions defending a fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime at a time when many traders said the real was over-valued. \par \par \uc2  Fraga joined the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated and vowed to respect market forces. \par \par \uc2  The Latin country also finalised an agreement with the IMF for a $41.5 million instalment loan. The accord stipulates that Brazil hold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at $23.3 billion net of loans from the IMF and the Bank for International Settlements. \par \par \uc2  With Brazil making payments on several external bond and loan obligations in the last few weeks, foreign reserves at year-end would be around $22.6 billion net of IMF and BIS loans, traders estimate, leaving the country slightly short of its agreed IMF target. \par \par \uc2  Brazil has been unable to attract additional foreign capital into the stock or debt markets or raise new cash in the international bond markets, forcing the government to buy dollars to meet payments on interest and maturing debt. \par \par \uc2  A $2 billion debt swap, exchanging Brady bonds for global bonds completed two weeks ago, was originally designed to include a cash component - that is sell bonds for cash. But the cash tranche had to be quashed as higher interest rates in the U.S. lowered investor appetite for emerging market assets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  IMF officials have declined to comment on Brazil's request for lower reserve limits. \par \par \uc2  ((-Emerging Markets Unit; 212 859-1562 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvar016a9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
