\par\par \b \uc2  Brazilian Real Seen Under Pressure Through Year-End \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mara Lemos \par \uc2 1,075 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 1999\par 15:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones Energy Service \par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real sent shivers down investors' spines this week as it dropped to BRR2.00 per dollar, and likely will cause more goosebumps in the months ahead. \par \par \uc2  Financing requirements and uncertainties over domestic and international economic trends will hinder a recovery for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at least until the end of the year, economists and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  For the second day running, the real on Wednesday hovered above the BRR2.00 per dollar rate, levels that hadn't been tested since March, at the height of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  "The pressure will continue. It is difficult to foresee any appreciation of the real in the short-term," said Carlos Geraldo Langoni, former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president and now director of the center for world economy at the Fundacao Getulio Vargas economics institute. \par \par \uc2  The real managed to close stronger Wednesday, at BRR1.9880 per dollar compared to BRR2.0020 Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened Thursday at BRR1.9910. \par \par \uc2  "The real will float between BRR1.90 and BRR2.00 (per dollar), depending on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's disposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more or less," Langoni said. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't offering any palliatives and has repeatedly stated it will remain out of the market. \par \par \uc2  Not that it has much of a choice, either. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is hamstringed by a commitment with the International Monetary Fund to keep Brazil's international reserves at $22.2 billion in October, excluding the $17.8 billion already received as part of an aid package. On Tuesday, Brazilian reserves stood at $40.035 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Private-sector financing requirements, which indicate the level of demand for the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are estimated at $500 million in October. These exclude obligations from the government, which usually taps reserves to make payments. \par \par \uc2  But with tight reserves, the Treasury was reportedly a buyer on Tuesday to meet commitments of around $3.35 million due this month, bearing the brunt of the blame for the real's weakness. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury on Wednesday denied it had instructed federally-run Banco do Brasil to purchase dollars on behalf of the government, as had been reported by local media. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       Financing, Politics, Economy A Drag On \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Until year-end, financing requirements will remain high, according to\par analysts, at $300 million in November and $2 billion in December, not\par including the government's needs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We know there will be pressure in these months and, as markets do, the\par December pressure is likely to be brought forward," said Sergio Machado, head\par of Banco Fator's treasury department.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It (the financing requirement) sort of creates a disposition for a more\par expensive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On top of the palpable pressure of financial obligations, the real is also\par reflecting the market stress over the uncertainty on political and economic\par developments both domestically and abroad.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While Brazil's political scenario is much calmer than in the last quarter,\par the government's attempts to push ahead with key structural reforms have born\par little fruit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Even with the excuse of the obligations due, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves tend to\par reflect the strength of the economy and the confidence in it," said Carlos\par Augusto Levorim, director at Oryx Asset Management in Sao Paulo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Doubts over whether Brazil will be able to achieve a sustainable fiscal\par adjustment remain and the chances of getting the fiscal reform approved this\par year are thinning, said Getulio Vargas' Langoni.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists also expressed concerns over the direction of the U.S. economy,\par projecting that a rise in interest rates there would further discourage\par investments in Brazil. At the same time, the rise could slow down the U.S.\par economy and hamper prospects at one of Brazil's main export client.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The domestic question mark relates to the management of the fiscal\par adjustment, while from abroad, if the U.S. economy deteriorates, it will catch\par Brazil at a fragile moment," Langoni added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par        Some Call For More \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For most of those interviewed, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  position of not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in the market isn't wise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This academic stance of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is extremely dangerous," said\par Fator's Machado. In his opinion, the claim that the market should be left\par alone to find its own exchange level doesn't bode well in a country such as\par Brazil, where the flow is very volatile.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Echoing his opinion is Pedro Thomazoni, fixed-income director at Lloyds\par Asset Management in Sao Paulo: "A floating exchange rate is a beautiful\par concept but it doesn't much fit reality in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which has to have some level\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because the flow isn't a constant one."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Observers pointed out that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's presence in the market would\par function as a guiding hand, besides imposing a sense of discipline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This (non-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) stance is threatening to turn the dollar into an\par asset-hedging tool which could then generate hysterical action" in the market,\par said Fator's Machado.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  let the market get this stressed over legitimate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par demand, but it has to remember that we no longer have a fixed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par control inflation," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While concerns over the inflationary pressure of a weak real abound,\par analysts agreed that, in the short-term, Brazil should be able to contain\par inflation as interest rates remain high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stance seems to be very cool because it is seeing\par inflation within the target, but all this rationale will be affected if\par inflation numbers change in the future," said Dalton Gardimam, chief economist\par at Credit Lyonnais in Sao Paulo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazil's benchmark lending rate stands at 19% per year, down from a peak 45%\par in March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After abandoning the exchange rate trading band in mid-January, Brazil\par adopted an inflation targeting system to guide monetary policy. The target for\par the current year is 8%, with a tolerance interval of two percentage points\par either way.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inflation indices released this week point to a growing pressure on consumer\par prices, with prices in Brazil's largest city of Sao Paulo rising 1.13% in the\par period Sep. 16-Oct. 15, the University of Sao Paulo's Economic Research\par Institute said Wednesday. This compares with the latest Sao Paulo CPI figure\par compares with inflation of 0.91% in September and 0.74% in August.\par -By Mara Lemos; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-813-1988; mara.lemos@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument nrg0000020010828dval02dh8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
