\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Profit-taking brakes Asia slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,037 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 1999\par 12:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 24 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took another beating on Friday before profit-taking brought respite in the London morning, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  In Latin America overnight Colombia's embattled peso crashed to the bottom of its trading band for the third day running despite frantic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real lurched back to the weak side of 1.90 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were steady to firmer, with the Czech and Slovak crowns both adding to recent gains. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled again for most of the Asian trading day as a patchwork of domestic factors compounded a broader regional retreat, worsened by widespread stock market losses on the back of Thursday's 1.95 percent drop on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking kicked in during the London morning, lifting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply off their lows, but analysts said the overall trend was still down. \par \par \uc2  "We could be seeing a little bit of a mini-crisis developing here," said Mitul Kotecha, emerging market economist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen a bit of retracement over our (London) morning but in Asian time we saw a lot more weakness. Things still look very vulnerable in the region." \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht remained under pressure beyond 41 to the dollar while the Philippine peso, which has been hanging onto the baht's coat-tails, slithered through its own psychological barrier of 41 to the greenback before edging back. \par \par \uc2  Thai Prime Minister Chaun Leekpai provided more soothing comments, saying the country had no intention of pegging the baht to the dollar or imposing Malaysian-style capital controls, but he said rising oil prices were complicating efforts to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah extended Thursday's slide to touch 8,900 to the dollar as student riots over a new security bill spooked the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded strongly after parliament issued hard-hitting recommendations to tackle the Bank Bali scandal, saying seven top officials including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and finance minister should face swift legal action. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the report itself was positive but it remained to be seen whether concrete action would be taken, while the implication of senior figures could aggravate popular anger and fuel unrest. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was closed for a local holiday, but the won followed the wider downtrend in offshore trade. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  poured a further $142.4 million of foreign reserves into defending the peso's trading band on Thursday and analysts questioned how long the band, one of only three left in Latin America, could survive. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again ended on the floor of the band, at 1,993.97 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Since September 10 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has haemorrhaged an estimated $290 million from net foreign reserves of some $8.24 billion to shore up the peso. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said it would hang on by its fingernails until what is expected to be an imminent new funding agreement with the International Monetary Fund. Others said the bank could be forced to scrap the band in a matter of days. \par \par \uc2  "We think that the exchange rate regime could be abandoned as early as next week, as soon as the IMF meetings are over," analysts at Chase Manhattan said in a note to investors, adding that the peso would weaken as a result. \par \par \uc2  Fears of another U.S. interest rate rise helped push Brazil's real back to the weak side of 1.90 to the dollar on Thursday, its lowest in just over two weeks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unmoved in the London morning but analysts saw further weakness when American markets opened. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty, often swayed by global factors, eased very slightly against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on general world stock market jitters. By 0845 GMT it was quoted around 0.5 percent above parity against 0.65 percent late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown stayed on the strong side of the key barrier of 36 to the euro, breached on Thursday on optimism that the economy is improving. ((Gill Tudor, London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6414, fax 583 7239, gill.tudor@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, \par \par \uc2  including the change versus late New York trade the previous day \par \par \uc2  and the change in the year to date. \par \par \uc2  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly \par \par \uc2  quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to \par \par \uc2  reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted \par \par \uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in \par \par \uc2  units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the \par \par \uc2  rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. \par \par \uc2  ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the \par \par \uc2  first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     35.93   35.98   -0.13%   3.25%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.28    4.26    0.29%   5.07%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 255.80  255.96   -0.06%   1.84%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 43.15   43.30   -0.35%   0.35%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 16,385  16,380    0.03%  49.63%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab   4.48    4.46    0.45%  13.99%\par South Africa\tab \tab    6.04    6.04   -0.11%   3.26%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    75.70   75.70    0.00%  22.89%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.279   4.263    0.37%   3.89%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab 460,660 460,990   -0.07%  45.89%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab    9.34    9.35   -0.05%  -5.08%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab  1.9040  1.9040    0.00%  57.73%\par Venezuela\tab \tab     626.50  626.50    0.00%  10.98%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab   528.70  528.70    0.00%  12.44%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore\tab \tab      1.707   1.716   -0.50%   3.08%\par Hong Kong\tab \tab      7.767   7.767    0.00%   0.27%\par China\tab \tab \tab    8.278   8.278    0.00%  -0.02%\par Indonesia\tab \tab      8,550   8,800   -2.84%   7.55%\par Thailand\tab \tab \tab 41.00   41.40   -0.97%  13.57%\par Philippines\tab \tab    40.88   40.80    0.20%   6.60%\par Taiwan\tab \tab \tab   31.68   31.68    0.00%  -1.31%\par South Korea\tab \tab    1,212   1,207    0.41%   2.28%\par India\tab \tab \tab    43.57   43.48    0.21%   2.54%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9o031kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shp