\par\par \b \uc2  Latin America  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Brazil Weak Despite Auction \b0\par\par\uc2  By Namju Cho \par \uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 18:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real was slipping mid-Thursday after opening stronger, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's continued auctioning off of dollar-linked notes that have supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few weeks. Bits of positive news on the domestic political front also failed to substantially boost the real. \par \par \uc2  Due to Hurricane Floyd, many New York offices are closing by 1 p.m. EDT. Fixed-income markets will be closed by 1 p.m. EDT, while the New York Stock Exchange will remain open. \par \par \uc2  At 12:15 p.m. EDT, the Brazilian real was trading at a mid-rate of BRR1.8800, compared with Wednesday's close of BRR1.8790. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had announced Friday it would steadily reduce the amount of dollar-notes it auctions, offered over double its daily average Thursday. \par \par \uc2  One New York-based trader said many market participants were simply rolling over their positions. Those snapping up new bonds are those whose notes matured today, he added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been offering dollars in the market by auctioning off dollar-linked notes, allowing market participants to hedge against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been able to support the real through the auction, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly hit a record-low of BRR2.00 on Aug. 20. The auction has allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  without directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Separately, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government scored a victory in Congress late Wednesday, after a debt relief proposal for farmers that would have drained the government's coffers by about BRR25 billion was shelved. \par \par \uc2  The move would have aggravated the country's growing fiscal deficit and hampered Brazil's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Mexico were closed Thursday for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, smaller Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly weaker. \par \par \uc2  The Peruvian sol, Ecuadorean sucre, Colombian peso and Chilean peso all weakened, while the Venezuelan bolivar was unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Below is a summary of regional exchange rates in late trading compared to one U.S. dollar: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                    Thursday(1615 GMT)  Wednesday(Close)\par Brazilian Real (BRR)          1.8800          1.8790\par Mexican Peso (MXN)            closed*         9.3150\par Venezuelan Bolivar (VEB)    624.0000        624.0000\par Peruvian Sol (PEN)            3.4170          3.4088\par Ecuadorean Sucre (ECS)   11,428.0000     11,365.0000\par Colombian Peso (COP)      1,977.0000      1,972.0000\par Chilean Peso (CLP)          524.8500        524.2000\par    *Markets in Mexico were closed for a holiday.\par    Note: Argentine Peso is fixed 1:1 against the U.S. dollar under a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board regime.\par    -By Namju Cho; 201-938-5692; namju.cho@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1653GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1093 1835 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9g06u