\par\par \b \uc2  Latin America  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Brazilian Real Slips \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1999\par 22:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Brazilian real slipped in volatile trading as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadily reduced the amount of dollar-linked notes it auctions off, in turn reducing the level of support the auctions had been giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 3:00 p.m. EDT, the Brazilian real was trading at a midrate of BRR1.8815 to the dollar, compared with Tuesday's close of BRR1.8790 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had announced it would reduce dollar-note auctions Friday, offered about half of its daily average Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The (dollar-notes) auction has sustained the real," said one U.S.-based trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been offering dollars in the market by auctioning off dollar-linked notes, allowing market participants to hedge against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been able to support the real through the auction, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly hit a record-low of BRR2.00 to the dollar on Aug. 20. The auction has allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  without directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  A congressional vote in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected later Wednesday on a bill seeking debt relief for farmers is another negative, one U.S.-based trader said. If approved, the motion would further drain the government's coffers and aggravate the country's ballooning fiscal deficit. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, smaller Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed. \par \par \uc2  The Venezuelan bolivar and the Colombian peso both gained strength, while the Ecuadorean sucre, Peruvian sol and Chilean peso lost against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Below is a summary of regional exchange rates in late trading compared to one U.S. dollar: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                           Wednesday(1845 GMT) Tuesday(Close)\par Brazilian Real (BRR)          1.8815          1.8790\par Mexican Peso (MXN)            9.3150*         9.3220\par Venezuelan Bolivar (VEB)    624.0000*       624.2500\par Peruvian Sol (PEN)            3.4088*         3.4038\par Ecuadorean Sucre (ECS)   11,430.0000     11,205.0000\par Colombian Peso (COP)      1,972.0000*     1,975.0000\par Chilean Peso (CLP)          524.2000*       523.8000\par    *Wednesday's close\par    Note: Argentine Peso is fixed 1:1 against the U.S. dollar under a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board regime.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Namju Cho; 201-938-5692; namju.cho@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2003GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1093 1835 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9f06ru0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
