\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Ctrl Bk Uses Dlr-Linked Bonds To Control  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 897 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1999\par 21:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--Backed into a corner as its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eschewed direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of virtually the only other tool at hand to ease pressure: dollar-linked bonds. \par \par \uc2  And if the pace of much-needed fiscal reform doesn't pick up in the capital Brasilia, observers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  could find itself increasingly reliant on this measure. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hit by the speed of the (real's) depreciation Friday, and so had to offer the bonds," said Odair Abate, chief economist at Lloyds in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  Abate added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have set the psychological barrier of BRR2.00 per dollar as an "informal target." \par \par \uc2  In a surprise move Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered BRR3 billion-worth of 'NBC-E' bills when exchange rates hit BRR1.9950 per dollar, the real's weakest point in almost five months. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly denied it has any floor or ceiling for exchange rates, stressing that it's concerned only with market volatility and liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The real rebounded to close Friday at BRR1.9250/dollar on the auction announcement Friday, however, and opened stronger again Monday at BRR1.8675/dollar. Market participants were unanmious in attributing the sharp rally to the NBC-E placements. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer BRR1.85 billion-worth of Friday's unsold bills later Monday, ahead of a scheduled BRR1 billion placement Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Placing the bills gives the market a hedge against exchange rate fluctuations, with players buying them up instead of spot or future dollars. \par \par \uc2  The return to offering NBC-Es - the last placement before last week was Aug. 6 - is seen as not only welcome, but necessary. \par \par \uc2  "The advantage in offering the NBC-Es is that it creates a mechanism for preserving international reserves," said Jaime Valdivia, Brazil sovereign debt strategist at Morgan Stanley in New York. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazil's international reserves stood at $42.069 billion Thursday.\par      Minimizing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Volatility To Control Inflation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As important as the placement of NBC-Es was the term of the bills.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut the maturity of the papers, which is extremely\par important, as the market doesn't want long-term credit risk," said\par Leonardo Veras, a fund manager at Rio de Janeiro-based brokerage Graphus\par Participacoes who welcomed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strategy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The second lot of bills offered Friday had a maturity of just under\par six months, as do the bills on offer Monday, compared with 12 months\par previously.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Abate and Valdivia both noted the restrictions on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par freedom to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Under the revised terms of the macroeconomic framework agreement with\par the International Monetary Fund, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can only spend up to\par $3 billion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  between July and the\par end of the year. That's less than half the $8 billion it had available\par for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the March-June period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "For the free-float (regime) to have any credibility, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par must be kept to a minimum," said Morgan Stanley's Valdivia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added that the high 21.50% yield paid Friday on the NBC-Es reflects\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's willingness to trade off higher interest rates for\par more stable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy is based on\par staving off the threat of inflation, which they say will return if\par exchange rates remain too high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazil's IPCA consumer price index rose 1.09% in July from the\par previous month, up sharply from the 0.19% increase in June over May. The\par government has set an end-1999 IPCA target of 8%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't be left to do it alone, they said. The\par government must do its part too, amid what appears to be waning\par popularity on the policy front.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The government has to convince Brazilian society that it's in a\par better situation now than it was six months ago," said Lloyds's Abate,\par referring to the depths of Brazil's crisis following the mid-January\par devaluation of the real.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Abate cited various factors that could weigh heavily on sentiment in\par the short term, including the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision on\par interest rates Tuesday and jitters over Ecuador's financial stability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ultimately, analysts said, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's most effective weapon in\par controlling volatility in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets is completely outside\par its control.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market needs fundamentals, and if nothing is approved, then\par there's no reason for any optimism," said a Rio trader, referring to\par fiscal reforms up for debate in Congress.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Congress returned from recess earlier this month with a full slate of\par fiscal measures on its agenda - including legislation that would limit\par spending in all levels of government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But many observers are skeptical the administration of President\par Fernando Henrique Cardoso can push through the belt-tightening reforms.\par Cardoso's popularity is languishing at all-time lows according to recent\par polls, which may futher embolden a Congress that is already divided in\par its support for the president.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts have said the country's credibility in the eyes of the\par international financial community rests on fiscal reforms being passed.\par -By Jamie McGeever (5521) 580-9394; jmcgeever@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-08-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1912GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1833 \par \par \uc2 Dokumen