\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Selic rate unchanged, no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1999\par 15:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Aug 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from adding or draining liquidity in the money markets on Friday, leaving the key Selic rate unchanged at 19.5 percent, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The bank did not need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because banks' positions are balanced," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally borrows or lends funds to keep the market Selic rate in line with its reference Selic rate, now at 19.5 percent, but this week it only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice as the market has been quiet. \par \par \uc2  The bank cut the rate from 21 percent July 28 at its monthly policymakers' Copom (Monetary Policy Committee) meeting, where it also shifted its bias on rates to neutral from easing. \par \par \uc2  Depending on banks' demand for cash, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can inch the market's Selic up or down in daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Selic is used as a benchmark in setting domestic government debt yields and consumer credit rates. \par \par \uc2  The bank has gradually lowered the Selic from a peak of 45 percent reached in early March as inflation remains under control following the country's steep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation in mid-January. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5532)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8k027jf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22