\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING DEBT-Steady despite Brazil worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 19 (Reuters) - Emerging debt prices were little changed on Thursday despite worries that Brazil could slip on its tough fiscal stance, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday for the first time in three months to defend the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has hit a five-month low on concern that President Fernando Henrique Cardoso faces mounting opposition to austerity measures needed to balance the budget. \par \par \uc2  Brazil jitters helped pull emerging debt prices down on Wednesday, but by 1150 GMT on Thursday the spread over comparable U.S. Treasuries on the benchmark J.P. Morgan EMBI+ index had edged in four points to 1,176. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's spread on the EMBI+ was seven points tighter at 1,118 and dealers in London said the country's "C" bonds were well bid around current levels. \par \par \uc2  At 1150 GMT the "C" bond was quoted 1/8 up on late New York levels at 59-1/4 bid. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody's careful but (concern over Brazil) doesn't seem to have affected prices today," said one trader at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is basically trading at yesterday's close." \par \par \uc2  The latest blow to Cardoso came on Wednesday when the Brazilian Congress passed a measure to speed up voting on a proposal to pardon farmers' debts with the central government. \par \par \uc2  Cardoso, who holds a presidential veto, has said he will oppose any pardon if it is approved in a vote next week. But analysts said he would continue to come under pressure over unpopular measures aimed at meeting fiscal targets with the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  "If Congress backs the farmers on this issue, Cardoso's fiscal reform will be perceived by the market as in trouble," Mike Noone, Latin America economist at Westdeutsche Landesbank, said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  Seemingly undeterred by the uncertain climate, Brazilian national development bank BNDES was set to issue a three-year bond of around 200 million euros ($211 million), possibly on Thursday, through ABN AMRO. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said BNDES hoped to price the deal at a premium of 100 basis points over Brazil's 800 million euro 2002 bond, but had been forced to revise initial terms after the sovereign bond fell 0.75 percentage points in the secondary market. \par \par \uc2  Among other emerging debt issues, traders said there was buying interest in Mexico's PAR bonds and Russia's longer-dated globals. \par \par \uc2  ** Following is a table of key emerging market debt prices, \par \par \uc2  including the change versus late New York trade the previous day \par \par \uc2  and the change in the year to date. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOND\tab \tab \tab \tab  LATEST  PREV   NET CHG  NET CHG\par .\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab    IN 1999\par ARG FRBs\tab \tab \tab \tab   83 1/8  83\tab  1/8     -2 3/8\par ARG GLOBAL 17\tab \tab \tab    85 3/8  84 3/4   5/8    -15\par BRAZIL C BOND\tab \tab \tab    59 1/8  59 1/8  0\tab     -3/8\par BRAZIL EI BOND\tab \tab \tab   74 1/2  74 1/4   1/4     10\par BRAZIL IDU\tab \tab \tab \tab 95 1/4  95 1/2  -1/4\tab 4 1/2\par BRAZIL GLOBAL 27     70\tab 69 3/4   1/4\tab 2 1/2\par BULGARIA IABS\tab \tab \tab    68 3/4  68 3/8   3/8\tab 1 1/8\par ECUADOR PDIS\tab \tab \tab     26 7/8  26\tab  7/8    -14\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREA GLOBAL 08     102 1/8 102 1/2  -3/8     -1 1/8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MEXICAN PARS\tab \tab \tab     71 3/4  72 1/8  -3/8     -6 1/2\par MEXICAN UMS 26\tab \tab \tab  108     