\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  confirms  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 00:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, Aug 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga confirmed the bank sold dollars for reais Wednesday due to a shortage of liquidity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Fraga told journalists the bank will also exempt foreign investors from paying a Financial Transactions Tax (IOF) on fixed-income investments and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deals, in a move which could lure dollars to the country. The real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to five-month lows against the dollar Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The market was completely illiquid, and therefore we thought it was time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something we haven't done for about three months," Fraga said. The official said the 0.5 percent IOF for foreigners could still be reinstated in the case of large capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said the bank is also going to extend to 360 days from 180 days the time period for exporters to receive special cash advances against anticipated foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  income. \par \par \uc2  Fraga said he expects foreign direct investment to reach a total $25 billion in 1999, saying a total of around $19 billion has been invested in the country so far this year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief predicted that Brazil's trade surplus will reach $7 billion next year, compared with an estimate of $1.5 billion for 1999. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves according to the international liquidity concept, which includes accounts receivable, are seen reaching $45.2 billion at the end of next year, compared with $38.9 billion at the end of 1999. ((Brasilia Newsroom, +55-61-314-1193)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8i024wd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
