\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Brazil cenbank moves to prop up sinking real. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shasta Darlington \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 00:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday and removed a tax on foreign investment in a bid to lure more of the precious greenbacks into the country and halt a slide in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has hit a 5-month low. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in three months, selling dollars in an unsuccessful effort to prop up Brazil's embattled real. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended down 1.4 percent at 1.906 per dollar, its weakest since March. \par \par \uc2  As mounting political fears roiled markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Arminio Fraga also announced that foreign investors will be exempted from paying a 0.5 percent financial transactions Tax (IOF) on fixed-income funds and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deals. \par \par \uc2  "The market was illiquid, and therefore we thought it was time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something we haven't done for about three months," Fraga said after markets closed. \par \par \uc2  The real has lost 5.4 percent of its value so far this month amid concerns that President Fernando Henrique Cardoso could face growing opposition to crucial but unpopular austerity measures needed to balance the budget. \par \par \uc2  Cardoso saw his popularity sink to all-time lows in August, fuelling speculation his political alliance could be undermined. The latest blow to his authority came earlier Wednesday when Congress passed a measure to speed up voting on a proposal to relieve a chunk of farmers' debt with the federal government. \par \par \uc2  Cardoso responded with a televised message to lawmakers and the thousands of agricultural protesters camped out in Brasilia. \par \par \uc2  "The government cannot agree. I will not agree with the pardon for those who are big debtors, especially when they are stubbornly disobedient debtors," he said in a speech at the presidential palace. \par \par \uc2  The measure paves the way for voting on a farm lobby bill, which proposes an effective write-off of between 40 percent and 60 percent of the face value of farmers' $13 billion debts with the government. \par \par \uc2  The government has offered counter-proposals in a bid to prevent voting on the bill, which would threaten Brazil's budget balancing targets. \par \par \uc2  The bill will not come up for debate until next week, and it likely to face a presidential veto. Still, initial support for the proposal sent markets into a tailspin Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The political climate is leaving a lot of people nervous about the fiscal situation," said Francisco Carlos Laje, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Banco Real. \par \par \uc2  "Brazil's fiscal targets with the IMF (International Monetary Fund) could be compromised," he added, referring to strict budget goals agreed to in exchange for a $41.5 billion rescue loan. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to prop the real up with dollar sales when it weakened beyond 1.9 per dollar for the first time in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  After markets closed, Fraga announced the tax changes and said the bank would extend to 360 days from 180 days the time period for exporters to received special cash advances against anticipated foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  income. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sao Paulo's benchmark Bovespa index\tab    also ended down 2.4 percent at 9689 points, its lowest close since March 12, dragging neighbouring Argentina's markets down with it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5408, shasta.darlington@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8i024h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
