\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  sets  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention \highlight\uc2  limits. \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1999\par 23:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, July 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot reduce the country's projected liquid foreign reserves by more than $3 billion each month in the second half of 1999, a top government official said Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The government can bring the reserves down by up to $3 billion from these projections for this whole period (the second half)," Finance Ministry Executive Secretary Amaury Bier said. The official projections look for liquid, or net foreign reserves of $23.8 billion in July and $26.3 billion in December. \par \par \uc2  The new guidelines form part of the government and the International Monetary Fund's latest revision of Brazil's economic performance under a $41.5 billion loan agreement. \par \par \uc2  Preliminary results for June show liquid reserves stood at $23.2 billion, Bier said. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's liquid reserves refer to its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves according to the international liquidity concept, which includes accounts receivable. It excludes loans from the International Monetary Fund, the Bank for International Settlements and the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Bier said the projections for net reserves are: $24.6 billion in August, $25 billion in September, $25.5 billion in October, $25.6 billion for November and $26.3 billion in December. \par \par \uc2  He said these projections could vary by $1 billion higher or lower, depending on disbursements from the Inter-American Bank of Development and the World Bank during the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  The official said the rules on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the second half would give the government "more space and liberty to act" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Under the agreement the country signed with the IMF in March following its devaluation in January, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  could only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with set amounts of money every month. \par \par \uc2  Bier said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  guidelines could be changed again when the loan agreement is next revised in September or October. \par \par \uc2  The government predicted a rate of 1.75 for the real to the dollar for December in the revision announced Monday. \par \par \uc2  ((Brasilia Newsroom, 55-61 314-1193)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv75053aj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
