\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 /Discontinue  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 -3: $3B Spent To End-May \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1999\par 22:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Gleizer reiterated that only part of the $8 billion IMF funds have been used so far in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The limits imposed (by the IMF) haven't been used," he said. He added, however, that they had a "very important impact on the market" by providing the perception that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a well defined monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  He also said Brazil may use its international reserves, about $44.5 billion currently, to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Of the total $8 billion, which may be used until end-June, Brazil had used "around $3 billion" until end-May, central banker Arminio Fraga said during an interview with foreign correspondents in Rio de Janeiro May 28. \par \par \uc2  Fraga also said the institution will continue with its stated aim of controlling wild fluctuations in real-dollar rates in the second half. \par \par \uc2  Fraga added he hoped \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market will become less frequent in the second half. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The real, which weakened to BRR2.20/dollar in February, has since\par stabilized between BRR1.65-BRR1.75/dollar. In late trading Tuesday, the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was quoted at a mid-rate of BRR1.7515/dlr.\par   -By Adriana Arai; 55-61 321-1224 or 965-6883;\par    aarai@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-06-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2022GMT\