\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Ends -2: Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In Liquid Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 1999\par 23:00\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--In rollercoaster trade Wednesday dominated by news about the resignation of U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, the Brazilian real (BRR) eventually ended unchanged from Tuesday's closing level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished at a mid-rate of BRR1.6550 to the dollar on a spread of BRR1.6540-1.6560/dollar, identical to Tuesday's close. The real had opened weaker Wednesday at BRR1.6640, on worries over potentialy sentiment-dampening local factors and political instability in Russia. However, it was the surprising news from the U.S. that dominated Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Immediately after Rubin's resignation was reported, the real weakened further to BRR1.67 per dollar. That was before the consensus that his nominated successor - Deputy Secretary Lawrence Summers - wouldn't rock the boat set in. Also aided by capital inflows and major dollar selling by Citibank and Credit Commercial de France in afternoon trade, the real rallied to BRR1.65 to the dollar before settling at Tuesday's finishing level. \par \par \uc2  "The market was pretty volatile today, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying (dollars) at around BRR1.65/dollar," said a dealer at Banco Real in Sao Paulo, noting that on local futures markets, dollar contracts for June delivery reached as high as BRR1,690 (per $1,000). \par \par \uc2  Players said traded volume in all areas of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets will likely total around $4.5 billion, slightly higher than recent daily averages. \par \par \uc2  -By Jamie McGeever (5521) 580-9394; jmcgeever@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  05-12-99 \par \par \uc2  1700EDT \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dv5c00up6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
