\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil/Malan/Rate -4: Warns Against Premature Optimism \b0\par\par\uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 22:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Regarding the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Fraga reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't seek to fix parameters for real/dollar quotes through its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We only provide liquidity. Previously, there was a shortage of dollars and more recently there's been a need for reals," Fraga said. "We don't set goals for the level of the real." \par \par \uc2  The real was trading at BRR1.76/dlr late Monday, which compares with over BRR2.20/dlr earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Fraga said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't used a large chunk of the $3 billion in international funding made available for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  may spend $2 billion in April, plus whatever's left over from March, and $1.5 billion in May and June each. Last week, Fraga said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become increasingly rare in the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  Malan said that a second disbursement, of about $9 billion, from the IMF-led credit line should be available to Brazil within the next few days. The IMF executive board is expected to approve the revised macroeconomic framework of the aid pact at a meeting Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The finance minister said that continued support from international lenders "shows confidence that Brazil can resolve its problems." \par \par \uc2  Malan added his meetings earlier this month between Brazilian officials and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heads and leading private sector bankers in the U.S., Europe and Japan were encouraging. Private bankers have almost unanimously agreed to maintain exposure to the country. \par \par \uc2  He noted, however, that the responsibility for restoring investor confidence rests on Brazil's shoulders. \par \par \uc2  "The responsibility is ours...The country is going in the right direction because of numerous positive efforts by our public and private sector," Malan said. "Credibility is gradually returning." \par \par \uc2  While the scenario has brightened, Malan once again warned - as he did last Friday at a meeting with financial sector heavyweights in Rio de Janeiro - against premature optimism by markets. \par \par \uc2  "We went very rapidly from a situation of complete pessimism to optimism these last few weeks," Malan said, noting that difficult times still lie ahead. \par \par \uc2  "It is exactly during a moment of crisis that we must have patience...There is no magic and no substitute for hard work," he said. \par \par \uc2  Monday marked the first public appearance for both Malan and Fraga in Brazil's financial capital of Sao Paulo since the terms of the IMF-led aid agreement were revised earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  The president of the Brazilian Federation Of Banks, Roberto Setubal, welcomed the country's two top economic policy makers, saying that Monday's event "represents the financial sector's complete support for the country's new economic program." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par About 500 bankers and financial sector leaders attended Monday's\par luncheon.\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; (55-11) 813-1988; swisnefski@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2037GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3t02gq2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\