\par\par \b \uc2  POLL - Outlook on Brazil's real  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  improves. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Noriko Yamaguchi \par \uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 18:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 24 (Reuters) - The outlook on Brazil's weakened \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is improving considerably as investors feel a devaluation-sparked crisis in Latin America's largest economy probably has bottomed out, a Reuters poll of economists showed Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The average forecast of the 26 economists polled predicted a real rate of 1.80 per dollar by the end of June, 10 cents stronger than the 1.91 projection in an earlier poll conducted a month ago. \par \par \uc2  The real, which is currently hovering around 1.85 to the dollar, should end the year at 1.71, in line with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) forecast of 1.70, the poll showed. \par \par \uc2  The economists, polled on March 22 and 23, specialise in Latin America and hold posts in banks and brokerages in Brazil, the United States and Britain. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the real, which is now 35 percent weaker since the government first relaxed its rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in mid-January, has already seen its worst level and was now on its way toward a gradual recovery. \par \par \uc2  "I think we saw the low for the real at 2.15. They've got the economic team in place, the policies look right, there's strong IMF support. There's a good chance the worst is over for the real," said Kevin Grice, economist at American Express in London. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment in the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market picked up earlier this month after the IMF and the government struck a new accord to free up the second tranche of a $41.5 billion financial bailout programme, which was assembled late last year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders also took heart from the change of presidency at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Arminio Fraga, who was former aide to billionaire George Soros. \par \par \uc2  Fraga, equipped with a fresh team full of market savvy directors, started aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the real and limit volatility. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters said however that persistent dollar outflows linked to a load of foreign debt maturity would likely keep a lid on the real's recently budding strength. \par \par \uc2  The real's recovery hinges on foreign capital inflows, a bulk of which major global investors guaranteed recently by vowing to restore precious credit lines to Brazil. \par \par \uc2  "It will be difficult to turn around the real's trend unless there is a lot of foreign investor inflow pumping into the market," said Felipe Garcia, economist at I.D.E.A. consultants in New York. \par \par \uc2  Garcia also cast doubt on the real's trend, once the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ammunition of $8 billion to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market ran out. The IMF allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  to spend up to $8 billion from its reserves and IMF funds until June. \par \par \uc2  While the 1.71 per dollar projection for the end of December was a big improvement from 1.86 for the same period in the previous poll, economists saw the real weakening again to 1.81 by March 2000. \par \par \uc2  Once the real reaches a certain equilibrium, speculative funds may flow back into the country, fuelling volatility, said Alexandre Bittencourt, economist at Banco Primus in Rio de Janeiro. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not leave the real alone, but it will probably start protecting foreign reserves and limit \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real could come under fresh pressure if the IMF's fiscal target of a primary budget surplus, excluding interest payments, of 3.1 percent of gross domestic product, is not met by the year's end, economists added. \par \par \uc2  "There is still scope for disappointment on the fiscal side. What they have to do is very politically contentious," said American Express' Grice. "It's crucial for (President Fernando Henrique) Cardoso and his administration to keep up the pressure on the Congress to keep up the reforms." \par \par \uc2  Poll participants were asked the following question. \par \par \uc2  (26 responses) \par \par \uc2  Where do you see the real trading against the dollar: \par \par \uc2  1) by June's end? average: 1.80/dlr, median: 1.80/dlr \par \par \uc2  2) by September's end? average: 1.73/dlr, median: 1.75/dlr \par \par \uc2  3) by December's end? average: 1.71/dlr, median: 1.70/dlr \par \par \uc2  4) by March 2000? average: 1.81/dlr, median: 1.71/dlr \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423, noriko.yamaguchi@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv3o09m7u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
