\par\par \b \uc2  Latin America  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Real, Mexican Peso Weaken \b0\par\par\uc2  By Namju Cho \par \uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 20:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Major Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker late Monday on profit-taking and an expected demand for dollars as a slew of Brazilian Eurobond maturities come due this week. \par \par \uc2  At around 1845 GMT, Brazil's real was trading at a mid rate of BRR1.855 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of BRR1.85-1.86, slightly weaker than Friday's close of BRR1.845/dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week as profit-taking surfaced after\par investors decided much of the good news out of Brazil had already been\par priced into the market.\par    "More positive news is hard to come by," said Kiran Datar, a Latin\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at ABN-Amro Bank in Chicago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again this week, according to\par market talk in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the real faces significant downside in the next few days,\par particularly as an estimated $400 million to $500 million in Eurobond\par maturities coming due this week, with the bulk of it due Friday. On top\par of that, demand for dollars increases at the end of the month to settle\par accounts, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The only upside, traders in Rio de Janeiro said, is a rule change in\par foreign funds last week that is expected to bring some foreign capital\par into the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Mexican peso was also losing steam after hefty gains last week. At\par around 1900 GMT, banking leader Banamex quoted the peso at a mid rate of\par MXN9.7070/dollar, compared with MXN9.6800 at Friday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 22-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1907GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1093 1835 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3m028zy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
