\par\par \b \uc2  BRAZIL  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  WEEK-Maturing debt caps real strength. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Noriko Yamaguchi \par \uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 16:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 22 (Reuters) - A mountain of maturing foreign debt may cap budding strength in Brazil's real this week, but volatility may be limited as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen jumping in if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spins out of control, experts said. \par \par \uc2  The real, which ended last week at its strongest closing level since February 5, or at 1.855 per dollar, started Monday a tad weaker at 1.87, pressured by corporate debt expiries of more than $1 billion scheduled until the end of March. \par \par \uc2  "The market will certainly be strained this week and next week due to the maturities," said Luis Cervenca, trader at Lloyds Bank in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  Bonds worth $275 million issued by Sao Paulo's water-sewer utility Sabesp  will come due on March 29, while some major bank bonds, each worth more than $100 million, are coming due this week and next. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the real/dollar rate to be stuck in the weaker end of a 1.80 to 1.95 per dollar range this week. \par \par \uc2  The real, which has lost 35 percent of its value since the government relaxed its rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in mid-January, started firming last week as investors became more confident Latin America's biggest economy was emerging out of its worst crisis in recent decades. \par \par \uc2  Some traders predicted the real would hold steady despite the pressure this week, or at least volatility would be limited, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps its recent vigil over the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "The pressure on the real this week seems to be smaller than expected earlier," said Sergio Machado, director of treasury at Banco Fator. "Many firms should have already bought their dollars and prepared for their expiries by last week. And despite the maturities, we expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have sufficient reserves to keep the market stable." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under a fresh agreement with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to free up a second tranche of last year's $41.5 billion financial bailout programme, has been allowed to spend up to $3 billion from its foreign reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this month. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves, which have been dwindling earlier this month as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  constantly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market supplying precious dollars, have actually grew late last week. \par \par \uc2  Reserves stood at $34.398 billion by Thursday, up from Wednesday's $34.386 billion. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, contrary to what it has been doing in recent weeks to support the real. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be replenishing its reserves after it sold millions of dollars from the country's reserves earlier in March, they said. \par \par \uc2  Still, the reserves, which serve as the country's main weapon against speculative attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were down $930 million from the start of March and down $1.712 billion from the beginning of February, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started reporting daily reserve levels. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423, noriko.yamaguchi@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv3m00v0q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
