\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's foreign reserves rise to $34.386 bln Wed. \b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 20:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 18 (Reuters) - Brazil's foreign reserves rose slightly to $34.386 billion by Wednesday from $34.355 billion Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not give a reason for the small growth. \par \par \uc2  Brazil lost $782 million from its reserves on Monday and Tuesday, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders speculated the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent dollars \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's reserves, the country's main weapon against speculative attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were down $973 million from the start of March and down $1.755 billion from the beginning of February, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  started releasing daily reserve levels. \par \par \uc2  Traders suspected the small increase in reserves reported on Wednesday was either due to the rise in value of some of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the bank owns or due to some inflows in the market. \par \par \uc2  Daily reserves may be accessed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's internet Web site of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcb.gov.br/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bcb.gov.br}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba00000200109