\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Focus: Horizon Brightens For Brazil's Real \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jamie McGeever \par \uc2 1,071 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 19:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real is on the cusp of stability after undergoing the most turbulent two months of its nearly five-year history, local analysts maintain. \par \par \uc2  Revised terms of a $41.5 billion multilateral credit line, significant government strides in its three-year fiscal adjustment plan and confidence in new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Arminio Fraga have all helped lift dark clouds of recent market pessimism. \par \par \uc2  Local market sentiment is now betting the real will strengthen to around BRR1.75 per dollar by the end of June after a dramatic "overshoot" in the wake of January's forced devaluation, according to three Brazil-based analysts consulted by Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  The real's recent performance is providing the best proof of the sudden optimism. At the height of market pessimism earlier this month, the real sank to a historic low of BRR2.22/dollar amid a perceived lack of definition on the policy front. It opened at a mid rate of BRR1.845 on Tuesday, building further on solid gains posted last week, when it closed at BRR1.91. \par \par \uc2  Rules governing \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets under last week's reworked economic framework with the International Monetary Fund has particulary pleased market watchers. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dollars to sell, so there will be less speculation (against the real)," predicted Alexandre Azara, chief economist at Bank BBA Creditanstalt in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Market Reacts Positively To \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rules\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has vowed to contain volatility in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par trading - and while it hasn't specified at what points it will do so, it\par has declared the volume of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds it has at its disposal\par through June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As reported, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may use up to $3 billion of IMF-led aid\par in March to maintain stability in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. Another $2\par billion may be spent in April, with $1.5 billion limits in both May and\par June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now has an impressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, and\par the real will surely not return to over BRR2.00/dollar," predicted\par Antonio Costa, head of fixed income Oryx Asset Management in Sao Paulo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The IMF is widely tipped to disburse the second tranche of last year's\par package in April, providing the market with a $9.2 billion liquidity\par injection to offset still negative capital flows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is a very credible policy," said Azara, who likens the IMF aid\par to a bridge loan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the near-term funds in place, inflation fears are also easing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Dow Jones Newswires survey of nine U.S. investment houses in late\par January pegged 1999 inflation at 28% - with Salomon Smith Barney and\par Lehman Brothers providing the most bearish estimates, at 35% and a\par whopping 80%, respectively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Fernando Henrique Cardoso's government has since set a\par provisional target of 16.8% inflation for 1999 under the revised IMF\par targets, and local analysts aren't scoffing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The inflationary peak has passed, and that peak was when the real was\par at BRR2.20 to the dollar," said Leonardo Freire, associate director at\par Warburg Dillon Read in Rio de Janeiro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Freier, Costa and Azara all described 15% as a reasonable estimate for\par inflation this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par         Inflation Fears Already Easing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In February, Brazil's IGP-DI index, a broad measure of wholesale,\par consumer and construction prices, rose 4.44% from a month earlier.\par Wholesale prices, which account for 60% of the index, jumped a\par higher-than-expected 6.99%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But with real-dollar rates on the slide, retailers will be less likely\par to pass on recent increased production costs to consumers, according to\par Freire.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Costa thinks inflation won't be quite the problem initially feared\par because of an expected recession.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government is predicting a 3.5% to 4% contraction in gross\par domestic product this year, after the economy grew a scant 0.15% in\par 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, financing prospects from other sources than the IMF are\par also looking brighter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Direct foreign investments this year - as much as $17 billion\par according to government estimates - are expected to finance Brazil's\par current account deficit, allowing companies to tap trade finance lines\par to kick-start exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the government's goal of replacing last year's $6 billion trade\par deficit with an $11 billion surplus in 1999 is considered overly\par optimistic by some observers, Freire, Costa and Azara see a surplus of\par $8 billion to $10 billion as attainable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government's 1999 deficit target on the current account front is\par 3% of GDP, down from 4.95% for the most recent 12 months ended January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In another positive development, leading commercial bankers in Europe,\par the U.S. and Japan have pledged to maintain February's trade and\par interbank lines through August after Finance Minister Pedro Malan and\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Fraga lobbied for such guarantees in a global\par roadshow that began last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Relatively Quick Return To Capital Markets Predicted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Once harvest exports start rolling in May and an estimated $5.2\par billion in foreign debt obligations over the next two months are met,\par analysts say real-dollar rates will begin to settle. That, in turn,\par should allow the country to tap international capital markets once\par again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Citibank Vice Chairman William Rhodes said Monday he was "very\par optimistic" Brazil would be able to access international markets before\par the end of April - not bad, considering Brazil's early bungled steps\par toward a free-floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in mid-January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If trade finance lines return, a sovereign government bond issue\par would be the benchmark for the private sector to enter the Eurobond\par market again, brightening the mood even more," said Oryx's Costa, noting\par the near-completion of the government's fiscal adjustment plan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The last piece in the policy jigsaw puzzle will be final Congressiona