\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil says 4 Japan banks to maintain lines to Aug. \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 15 (Reuters) - Four Japanese banks agreed on Monday to maintain their interbank and trade lines with Brazil until August 31 at the same levels as at the end of February, a senior Brazilian official said. \par \par \uc2  Marcos Caramuru, secretary for international affairs at the Finance Ministry, said the banks were Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi , Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank , Sanwa Bank  and Sumitomo Bank . \par \par \uc2  Sergio Werlang, director of economic policy at Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the real was "completely undervalued" but that Brazil would seek to boost the real's value through sound macroeconomic policies, not through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The real exchange rate in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  is way off - too devalued," he said. \par \par \uc2  But he said Brazil's agreement with the IMF called for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to control volatility, not to boost the rate of the real against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, I think the market's expectations are overblown - pessimistic," Werlang said. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to convince them we're right," as the results of inflation and debt reduction programmes emerge. He added that January and February data looked favourable, but he did not provide specifics. ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv3f02z3q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
