d in the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Figueiredo was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday, a day after the new IMF terms and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  figures\par were announced, the real (BRR) strengthened to BRR1.88 per dollar from\par Monday's close of BRR1.98/dlr. The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened trading\par Wednesday at BRR1.87/dlr. Before the free-float in mid-January, the real\par was quoted at BRR1.21.\par         Breadth Of Information Well-Received\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts also welcomed the disclosure Monday of the economic framework\par for the $41.5-billion aid package. The new agreement with the IMF made\par public all the macroeconomic variables used in the model and expected\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  quotes against the dollar each month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We had zero idea of what the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's parameters for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were before," said Christian Stracke, economist at BT Alex\par Brown in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For Barros, the government introduced a little "predictability" in the\par performance of international reserves and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates,\par essential for private-sector decision-making.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "And most importantly, the government didn't water down the free-float\par regime," Barros added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Finance Ministry's economic policy secretary Amaury Bier said\par Tuesday that there will be two types of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One, with the IMF's $8 billion, aims to cover Brazil's current account\par deficit during four months of an expected sharp shortage of dollars. The\par other, Bier said, has no pre-set limits and is a type of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par designed to control excess volatility, using what is left of Brazil's\par reserves - at $34.572 billion Monday.\par      Dollar Inflows Expected From Investment, Trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to calculations by BBV's Barros, Brazil's public- and\par private-sector foreign commitments tally up to $4.385 billion in March.\par That figure includes bonds coming due, amortizations, interest,\par repatriation of profits, and other loans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't think Brazil will have to use all the $3 billion this month,"\par he said, estimating there will be around $1 billion a month in foreign\par direct investment and 10% to 20% of debt rollover. It's "too naive" to\par think that "dollar inflows have dried completely," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The margin is comfortable, and Brazil may save some of March's\par munition for April, when the pressure on the real will be bigger," he\par said, without revealing his calculations for next month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To restore dollar inflows, the government is counting on the return of\par foreign credit lines to Brazilian companies and a sharp turnaround in\par its trade balance - to an $11 billion surplus in 1999 from a $8.4\par billion deficit last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most analysts think the $11 billion surplus goal is overly ambitious,\par but they agree exports will pick up fast, becoming the short-term\par supplier of dollars in the market aside from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In February, Brazil posted its first real trade surplus, totaling $219\par million, since May 1996 - real because in June 1998 technical factors\par generated a small surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Barros estimated that the trade surplus will stand around $400 million\par in March, $700 million in April, and will surpass the $1 billion mark in\par May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Until the end of the year, exports should outpace imports by $7.9\par billion," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BMC's Allain is more optimistic about the second half of the year,\par when he believes the supply and demand for dollars will even out.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There may be four, five months which may not be so positive, when\par foreign debt commitments must be met," he said. "But in the second half,\par an improving trade balance and lower debt burden will lead to a more\par balanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As a result of the improved trade balance figures, Brazil's current\par account deficit is expected to shrink to 3%-3.3% of GDP in 1999,\par according to analysts, from last year's 4.5%.\par  -By Adriana Arai and Jamie McGeever; 5561-321-1224; aarai@ap.org\par (Michelle Wallin in Buenos Aires contributed to this article.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1453GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1833 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3a01wue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
