\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging debt firms amid optimism over Brazil. \b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 19:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 10 (Reuters) - Emerging market bond prices rose sharply on Wednesday amid a flurry of positive news on Brazil this week including the promise of fresh funds from the International Monetary Fund (IMF), traders and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Optimism about the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy as well as approval on Wednesday of a key fiscal bill by the country's lower house that would raise the financial transactions tax also buoyed prices. \par \par \uc2  Market experts said they expected Brazil's new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Arminio Fraga to get a warm response from investors during his foreign tour which begins on Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  "The market is being driven higher by continued optimism over what Arminio has been able to put in place so far in Brazil," said one head trader at a U.S. investment bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  "I expect he will get a favourable response," the trader added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1300 EDT/1800 GMT, benchmark Brazil C bonds\tab \tab   were one percentage point higher at 60-1/8 and its global bonds due 2008 were 1-1/2 stronger at 72-3/4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the real, rose 1.1 percent by midday to 1.87 reais per dollar on talk the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier news that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to return to the foreign debt markets after it receives a second instalment of $9.2 billion in loans from an IMF-led rescue package was viewed favourably but some analysts said Brazil still would have to pay a high price to reenter international capital markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It would be great if they could do that but do they want to sell debt at the 15 percent level that I think the market would require?" said one emerging market debt strategist at a U.S. investment bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There are a lot of people underweight Brazil that may be compelled to come back into the market because prices have done better so conceivably there would be some demand," the source said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the analyst said a lot would depend on the size and maturity of the issue and he noted that even a five-year issue would have to come in at around 13 percent to get the deal done.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One source said market rumours were that Brazil may try to come with up to $5.0 billion in the international capital markets after they receive the IMF funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, market sources said Panama is expected to price a $500 million global bond issue on Thursday through underwriter BankBoston, which declined to comment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the broader secondary Latin market, prices were also firmer on the positive news from Brazil. Argentine FRBs bonds\tab \tab  were 1/2 higher at 84-5/8 bid and Mexican PAR bonds\tab \tab  were 1/4 firmer at 77-1/8.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, Russian debt prices rose on renewed hopes of a breakthrough on talks between Russia and the IMF.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Russian global bonds due 2005\tab \tab    rose two percentage points to 22 bid and the country's global bonds due 2018\tab \tab    firmed 3-3/4 to 23-3/4 bid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (( Diane Craft, Emerging Markets Unit, 212-859-1728 )).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv3a05rj2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
