\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's real opens firmer at 1.86/dlr - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 14:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  real opened 1.86 per dollar Wednesday, 1.6 percent firmer from Tuesday's close of 1.89, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real ended at its strongest closing point in a month on Tuesday, following an announcement from the government and the International Monetary Fund (IMF) that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with more funds to support the real. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the government announced the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was allowed to use up to $8 billion until June to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to supply dollars and meet heavy U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand from Brazilian firms paying off foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  Late on Tuesday, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director said Brazil can also use $1 billion from its World Bank loans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as they were beyond the limits agreed with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  Prospects of the additional cash in markets were being cheered by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  players, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Some $6.5 billion in corporate Eurobonds were expected to come due between March and June this year, analysts noted. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423, saopaulo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par 