\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil real ends firmer at 1.89 to dollar - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 21:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 9 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed 4.8 percent to 1.89 per dollar on Tuesday after the International Monetary Fund and the government reached a new accord that set rules on \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, closed at its strongest against the dollar in a month, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Under the fresh accord with the IMF, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may now use up to $8 billion from the country's foreign reserves and IMF funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets until June, supplying dollars to help support the real. \par \par \uc2  The real, at 1.89, has lost 36 percent of its value against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the government relaxed its tight \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy on Jan. 13. \par \par \uc2  "Markets received the new measure well," said Marcelo Allain, economist at BMC Bank in Sao Paulo. "The measure will at least serve as a bridge for a market suffering from a huge demand for dollars." \par \par \uc2  Markets were recently parched of dollars as Brazilian companies sought U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay off their maturing foreign debt. Allain estimated that some $6.5 billion in Eurobonds were coming due between March and June. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, though a foreign firm carried out a deal to bring about $100 million into the country, which helped the real to firm in late trading. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the benchmark overnight Selic rate ended at 45 percent a year after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled rates at that level in its morning auction Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Interest rate futures traded on the BM&F Futures and Commodities Exchange ended mixed. Rates were projected to rise to 43.89 percent by the end of March, against Monday's projection of 43.02 percent. They were seen at 40.80 percent by the end of April, down from Tuesday's projection of 44.46 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423, saopaulo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv39072e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
