\par\par \b \uc2  ADR REPORT - Emerging market highlights - March 8. \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 22:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LATAM ADRS AIDED BY REVISED IMF PLAN FOR BRAZIL \par \par \uc2  By Daniel Bases \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 8 (Reuters) - Latin American ADRs - American Depositary Receipts - strengthened Monday after the the International Monetary Fund issued its hotly anticipated set of new financial conditions for Brazil's loan package. \par \par \uc2  The lending agency said it agreed to a revised economic programme for Brazil that would lead to the release of $4.9 billion, the second tranche of a $41.5 billion line of credit. \par \par \uc2  Latin American ADRs were solidly higher before the revised plans were made public and gained more ground afterward. \par \par \uc2  Telephone issue, Telebras , the main bellwether stock for the region, was up 2-1/16 at 69-15/16 in New York. \par \par \uc2  "This market is just ridiculously cheap right now. (Arminio) Fraga is saying the right things. They've got the deal with the IMF and for the short-term. Their debt payment schedule looks lighter," said one senior LatAm trader. \par \par \uc2  Fraga, Brazil's new \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, said the country's annual inflation rate should be between five and 10 percent in 2000 and, hopefully, down under five percent in 2001. \par \par \uc2  Under the IMF's revised loan programme, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  will set limits for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sees the real, the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trading at 1.70 to the U.S. dollar by the end of this year. \par \par \uc2  The real was trading at 1.970 per U.S. dollar in late afternoon trade in New York. \par \par \uc2  Under the agreement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may spend up to $3 billion in March, $2 billion in April and $1.5 billion in May and again in June to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The accord is good and it came at the right time," said Dany Rapapport, economist with Banco Santander in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazil's benchmark stock index, the Bovespa\tab    gained ground after the announcement of the conditions and was trading up 3.39 percent.\par The ING Barings Latin American ADR index\tab   was up 2.09 points, or 1.76 percent, at 120.75.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Here are some other emerging market highlights:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ***\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BRAZIL - Embratel Participacoes , a provider of domestic and long-distance phone services, was up 1-3/16 at 15-7/16. Tele Centro Sul , another phone service provider, was up 1-3/16 at 41-7/16 and cellular phone service provider Telmig Celular  was up 1-5/16 at 20-15/16.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ***\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MEXICO - Telefonos de Mexico\tab      , Mexico's bellwether telephone stock, was up 2-3/8 at 60-11/16. Grupo Televisa SA de CV\tab \tab was up 2-1/8 at 30-5/8.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Wall Street Desk 212-859-1730)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv3800sw8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
