\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Cenbank sells dlrs to support real - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 21:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday afternoon, selling dollars to prevent the real from weakening further, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , through particular banks, sold dollars at 2.16 reais per dollar, managing to maintain the real at that level, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real opened its afternoon session at 2.19 per dollar, a tad firmer compared with its morning low of 2.2. \par \par \uc2  The real seemed to stick to 2.16 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened earlier in the day due to dollar outflows from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which were a result of Brazilian companies paying off maturing debt, traders said. Some $2 billion in foreign corporate bonds were expected to come due this month. \par \par \uc2  The real has lost 44 percent of its value since the government relaxed its rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy on January 13. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv3303e83\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
