\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Ctrl Bk/Rate -2: Committee To Discuss Rates Thu \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 13:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market to set its overnight rate, known as Selic, at 39%, a spokesman at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily on the interbank market to set rates since Jan. 19, one day after its Monetary Policy Committee, known as Copom, raised the ceiling rate at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may lend to banks to 41% from 36%. The interbank rate stood at 29.80% on Jan. 18 and has remained at 39% since Feb. 1. \par \par \uc2  Last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president nominee Arminio Fraga, who should receive final Senate approval Wednesday, said that interest rates will remain high in the short term, as long as the transitory effects of the country's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation are in effect. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real (BRR), has lost 44% of its value against the dollar since Jan. 13, when the government first loosened restrictions on exchange rate fluctuations. On Tuesday, the real closed at a mid-rate of BRR2.16/dollar, its weakest closing mark ever. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised banks' compulsory deposit requirements in a move to "dry up liquidity and, consequently, relieve pressure on the real." A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source said that the measure should trim liquidity by BRR5 billion to BRR6 billion. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Copom is scheduled to meet Thursday to discuss interest rates.\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; (55-11) 813-1988; swisnefski@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1254GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3301nf1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
