\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Brazil tries to rein in record-low real. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shasta Darlington \par \uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 18:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets again on Tuesday to prop up the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it tumbled to a record low, threatening to throw Latin America's biggest economy deeper into crisis. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverted to selling dollars on Tuesday after a day on the sidelines in order to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which bottomed out at a record intraday low of 2.22 reais per dollar. By midday the real had inched up to a still-fragile 2.16 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We're playing with fire," Augusto Lopez-Claros, an economist at Lehman Bros. in London, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "If confidence doesn't return to Brazil following the approval of the IMF programme there will be serious implications for the economies of the region and the whole continent," he said. \par \par \uc2  The government is hammering out new fiscal targets with the International Monetary Fund in an attempt to prevent the devaluation, which has already topped 40 percent, from spinning out of control. \par \par \uc2  A further slide could spark flyaway inflation and another hike in already crippling interest rates. The government's National Statistics Institute said on Tuesday that unemployment hit a record high of 7.73 percent in January as Brazil heads in to what is likely to be its worst recession in decades. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said talks with Brazilian officials should result in some "good news" in coming days but full details of a new rescue deal were only expected by mid-March. \par \par \uc2  Reserves fell by a slim $102 million during the first two days of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week. Massive dollar outflows forced \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  to float its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  six weeks ago, undermining initial targets set last year and sending the government back to the negotiating table with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  Markets are hoping new targets will pave the way for more financing options - and therefore greater access to sorely-needed dollars - as well as the next instalment of the $41.5 billion rescue loan to bolster Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  Pessimism reigned in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, however. A fundamental lack of dollars combined with dwindling investor confidence in the government's ability to sidestep an economic crisis put further pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "In the short term, with a lack of decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and dollar flows, the real should continue to be under pressure," said Mauro Schneider, chief economist at ING Barings Bank in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  Arminio Fraga, a former aide of billionaire financier George Soros, is expected to be confirmed this week by the Senate as the new president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing him to get on with the formation of a concrete \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Some economists forecast Fraga will further raise interest rates at a meeting of the bank's Copom monetary policy committee on Thursday to help rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand is strong as some $2 billion in corporate Eurobonds come due this month and as importers snap up greenbacks to pay for their goods. Exports, on the other hand, have been seriously hampered because foreigners are unwilling to lend Brazilians cash. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said export financing has shown signs of picking up and a glimmer of hope appeared Monday when Brazil announced a monthly trade surplus of $219 million in January - its first since June 1998. \par \par \uc2  But concern that support for the government's crisis drive could be waning also put pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The lower house of Congress is due to vote this month on a higher financial transactions tax that is a key part of the plan. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv3203ckt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
