\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Ctrl Bk -2: Interbank Rate At 39% Since Feb. 1 \b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 13:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market to set its overnight rate at 39%. \par \par \uc2  The rate, known as the Selic, has remained steady at that level since Feb. 1. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily on the interbank market to set rates since Jan. 19, one day after its Monetary Policy Committee (Copom), raised its ceiling lending rate to 41% from 36%. The interbank rate stood at 29.80% on Jan. 18. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president nominee Arminio Fraga told a Senate committee that interest rates will remain high in the short term, as long as the transitory effects of the country's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation are in effect. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, has lost 43% of its value against the dollar since Jan. 13, when the government first loosened restrictions on exchange rate fluctuations. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Copom is scheduled to meet late Thursday to discuss interest\par rates.\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; (55-11) 813-1988; swisnefski@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1230GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3201n4p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
