\par\par \b \uc2  Brady Bonds Down On The Back Of A Weaker Brazilian Real \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 17:34\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Brady bonds are weakening mid-morning Tuesday, as the Brazilian real heads south, pulling emerging debt along. \par \par \uc2  After a strong opening, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened and then slightly recovered mid-morning at BRR2.15/dlr versus BRR2.17/dlr earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  The real traded at BRR2.19/dlr on a spread of BRR2.18-2.200/dlr Tuesday morning, compared with an opening quote of BRR2.10/dlr and Monday's closing of BRR2.13/dlr. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased off its lows due to an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank would neither confirm or deny that it had entered the market. \par \par \uc2  The country's C-bonds dropped 5/8 to 55 1/2 bid, while the EIs lost a point to 61 1/4 bid. \par \par \uc2  Argentine Pars are down 3/4 to 66 bid and the FRBs declined 5/16 to 81 11/16 bid. \par \par \uc2  Mexican debt, however, escaped most of the downdraft. The country's Pars were up 1/4 to 74 3/4 bid, while the UMS 2026s were 1/4 higher to 105 bid. The Discounts inched 1/8 higher to 81 1/2 bid. \par \par \uc2  "People like Mexico better than Brazil. It's a better story," a trader said, referring to its outperforming sovereign debt. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As a nervous real causes some jitteriness in the market, investors\par anxiously await the terms of a new economic policy agreement between\par Brazil and the International Monetary Fund. Also, Thursday's meeting of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b