\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Cenbank sells dlrs again, at 2.16 reais. \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 16:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Tuesday while the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  careened to a record intraday low, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at 2.16 reais after the real was offered at a record low of 2.22 reais, traders said, allowing the real to firm back to 2.17 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had tried in vain to contain the real's slide by selling dollars at 2.10 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no comment to make on the market's information about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, while last week it had announced on several occasions that it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not appear in the market despite the 5 percent depreciation in the real to a record-low close of 2.15 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders and economists attribute the real's recent weakness to a shortage of dollars and foreign debt obligations. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5537)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv3203jpu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
