\par\par \b \uc2  Brazilian Mkts Still Unsettled As Another Key Week Begins \b0\par\par\uc2  By Stephen Wisnefski \par \uc2 1,001 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 21:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazilian markets finally got the dose of good news they were craving Friday, but an assortment of unknowns continued to quell investor confidence as yet another crucial week got underway Monday. \par \par \uc2  "There's just not any interest in our market, and I don't see it picking up from one day to the next," said a fund manager at one Sao Paulo investment bank. "We still have a number of issues that have the potential to hurt the market, but none that really could give it a boost this week." \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president nominee Arminio Fraga easily won approval from the Senate's economic affairs committee. Fraga and five new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directors are expected to breeze through final confirmation in a vote Wednesday in the Senate plenum. \par \par \uc2  Also Friday, tensions between President Fernando Henrique Cardoso and several recalcitrant governors - embroiled in a spat over state debt obligations - eased after a meeting between the two sides. The federal government refused to restructure existing debt contracts but did agree to some concessions. \par \par \uc2  Both events were seen as positive steps in the process to heal crippled credibility, but Brazil faces several more tests this week, and markets remain volatile as a result. \par \par \uc2  In late trading Monday, the real (BRR) weakened to BRR2.13/dlr late, compared to Friday's close of BRR2.035/dlr and an opening Monday of BRR2.02/dlr. Traders said a scarcity of exports, combined with importers rushing to close exchange contracts, were pressuring the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The benchmark index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange, or Bovespa, was up 3.2% to 9192 in paper-thin trading. \par \par \uc2  "There's no volume so this isn't the start of an upward trend," the fund manager said, noting that investors will remain on the sidelines until the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market calms. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Monetary Policy Eyed \par \par \uc2  Financial markets are hopeful that Fraga's final approval will pave the way for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to clarify its plans for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy. Analysts, however, aren't convinced such information will be forthcoming. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people have been talking about having specific rules for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we're not expecting (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to announce any formal mechanism yet," said Constantin Jansco, an economist at MCM Consultores in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  Last week, Fraga said during his testimony that the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies that work best are those that are closest to being pure. He declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would announce formal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  adopted a free-float exchange policy in mid-January, which has resulted in a weakening of the real of more than 40% against the dollar. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on the exchange market to bolster the real for the first time since the free-float. \par \par \uc2  "Perhaps (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will tinker with some regulations on capital movements, but the moment you announce specific \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules, the market will test them immediately," Jansco added, noting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have enough reserves to determine under what circumstances it will always \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the real. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves stood at $35.6 billion last Friday, down from $44.6 billion at the end of 1998. \par \par \uc2  On the monetary policy front, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee, or Copom, is scheduled to meet late Wednesday to discuss interest rates. The group last met on Jan. 18, when it raised the ceiling rate at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may lend to banks, known as the Tban, to 41% from 36%. \par \par \uc2  Since then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily on the interbank market to set overnight rates. The interbank rate, which stood at 29.80% before the last Copom meeting, has remained at 39% since Feb. 1. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we'll see any rate changes coming out of the Copom meeting. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pretty clear that they'll keep them steady," said Jansco. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Fraga said during his Senate appearance that, while rates could fall in the medium term, the government must maintain a strict monetary policy to contain the effects of the devaluation. The new central banker said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's primary aim is to protect the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prevent the return of hyper-inflation. \par \par \uc2  IMF Accord Revision, New Budget Cuts Expected \par \par \uc2  Markets are also anxiously awaiting an announcement from the Brazilian government and the International Monetary Fund on the revised terms of the $41.5 billion IMF-led aid deal inked last November. A team of Brazilian officials has been in Washington for the past two weeks hammering out the details of the agreement. IMF Managing Director Michel Camdessus said Monday a new agreement is likely in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  The revised accord should include new macroeconomic targets. Brazil is expected to respond by announcing a series of additional budget cuts, of up to BRR7 billion, according to market estimates. \par \par \uc2  Brazil, which already has received $9.4 billion in funding, hopes to draw down a second tranche of about the same amount before the end of this month. \par \par \uc2  Finally, while progress was made on the state debt talks, Minas Gerais Governor Itamar Franco - who set the battle in motion on Jan. 6 by declaring a 90-day moratorium on debt payments to the federal government - continues to be a thorn in Cardoso's side. \par \par \uc2  Franco, the only one of Brazil's 27 governors who didn't participate in last Friday's meeting, hinted over the weekend that the state might extend the moratorium. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Monday, the Minas Gerais governor was in Brasilia meeting with\par Senators from his party - the government-allied Democratic Movement\par Party - and opposition party members in the lower house, but has so far\par declined to meet with Cardoso.\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; (55-11) 813-1988; swisnefski@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2053GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1813 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3101o3w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
