\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again, real firms. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Noriko Yamaguchi \par \uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1999\par 19:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Feb 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fragile real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inched up to 2.04 per dollar at midday Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, supplying dollars for the third straight day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars in markets through particular banks at 2.04, a tad firmer against Wednesday's close of 2.05, to prevent the real from weakening again, traders said. Wednesday's 2.05 was the real's second weakest closing ever. \par \par \uc2  Pressure had increased Thursday when one big bank was seen scrambling for about $200 million in the market to pay off its maturing foreign debt, traders noted. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after two straight days of it (until Wednesday), is no longer a novelty," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Sao Paulo. "But now markets know that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would support the real if it threatens to go out of control." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling dollars quietly via dealers on Tuesday as the real ratcheted past the 2.00 psychological barrier. The real has now lost 40.7 percent of its value since the government was forced to devalue in mid-January. \par \par \uc2  The Bank finally decided to step into markets after more than a month of absence following the devaluation, because local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were recently parched for dollars, with about $3.8 billion in foreign debt expiring in February and March. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to traders, was trying to avoid a repeat of a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  nightmare seen on Jan. 29, widely known as "Black Friday". \par \par \uc2  A massive wave of foreign loan expiries put enormous pressure on the real/dollar exchange rate then and the real tumbled to its worst level ever of 2.1 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Market analysts estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now spent somewhere between $50 million and $100 million through Wednesday with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Actual figures were expected to be reflected in the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the coming days. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now reports on international reserves on a daily basis. \par \par \uc2  While the amount of the dollar sales was considered small, some economists sounded an alarm at \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's random \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It would have been wiser for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point," said Charles Blitzer, chief international economist at Donaldson, Lufkin & Jenrette in London. \par \par \uc2  Blitzer said any commitment by a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would slowly eat away at reserves and eventually raise doubt on whether the country would be able to withstand further speculative attacks in the markets. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's foreign reserves stood at $35.74 billion by Tuesday, down from $36.11 billion at the beginning of the month. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423, noriko.yamaguchi@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2p03tys\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
