\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKETS  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - E. Europe hit by econ fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1999\par 12:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 25 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker in thin trade on Thursday as fears of an economic slowdown in the euro zone weighed on eastern Europe. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also a focus following two straight days of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the real by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  By 1040 GMT, the Hungarian forint had sagged by nearly 1.0 percent and the Polish zloty was 0.70 percent weaker. \par \par \uc2  "Euroland growth is being revised downward and that is what is hurting the eastern European markets," said Mark Rall, emerging markets strategist at HypoVereinsbank Research in Munich. \par \par \uc2  "People are lowering expectations of export-driven growth out of eastern Europe." \par \par \uc2  Two German states reported disappointing consumer price data on Thursday and French business confidence figures fell. \par \par \uc2  This exacerbated fears over growing current account deficits in eastern Europe, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment toward Hungary faces a test on Thursday at an auction of two-and five-year government bonds, Rall said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors are expected to remain sidelined and this could exacerbate falls in Hungarian debt. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's shaky real was at 2.02 against the dollar, unchanged from Wednesday's European close but up from its $2.05 Sao Paolo close. \par \par \uc2  Brazil reported rising consumer price inflation on Thursday, heightening concerns that capital will seek to exit the real. \par \par \uc2  The nomination of new \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Arminio Fraga is up for a confirmation vote by lawmakers on Friday, a test the market is keen to be past. \par \par \uc2  For the time being, investors are avoiding the real and seeking to anticipate the effects of any further falls on outlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Gerry Celaya of American Express Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "Right now the peripheral markets are ignoring Brazil but if Brazil gets hit they will catch a sniffle," Celaya said. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso was up marginally from its Wednesday European close but the Venezeulan and Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed, with falls in the Korean won and Singapore dollar but small gains in the Thai baht and Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said losses on Wall Street on Wednesday had set a bad tone for Asia. \par \par \uc2  Asian markers were sitting tight before a news confernece by Japanese Vice Finance Minister Eisuke Sakakibara scheduled for 1200 GMT, they said. \par \par \uc2  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange \par \par \uc2  rates, including the change versus late New York trade the \par \par \uc2  previous day and the change in the year to date. For the latest \par \par \uc2  live prices click on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  RICs. \par \par \uc2  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the \par \par \uc2  euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted \par \par \uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted \par \par \uc2  in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the \par \par \uc2  rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. \par \par \uc2  ** Annual percentage changes are now calculated from late on \par \par \uc2  the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \uc2  ABRIDGED VERSION FOR \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  REPORT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   "LATESTFX"     "PREVCLOSE"  PCT CHG "PCT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHGON YEAR"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     37.96   37.93   0.08%   9.07%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.30    4.27   0.69%   5.59%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 252.29  251.03   0.50%   0.44%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 43.90   43.88   0.04%   2.09%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 12,900  12,800   0.78%  17.81%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab   3.82    3.83  -0.26%  -2.80%\par South Africa\tab \tab    6.21    6.19   0.20%   6.15%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    63.70   63.70   0.00%   3.41%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.053   4.045   0.21%  -1.60%\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   LATAM\par Mexico\tab \tab \tab    9.93    9.94   -0.08%  0.94%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab  2.0200  2.0200    0.00% 67.34%\par Venezuela\tab \tab     576.01  576.01    0.00%  2.04%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab   495.00  495.00    0.00%  5.27%\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   ASIA\par Singapore\tab \tab      1.727   1.726   0.09%   4.29%\par Hong Kong\tab \tab      7.748   7.748   0.00%   0.03%\par China\tab \tab \tab    8.279   8.279   0.00%   0.00%\par Indonesia\tab \tab      8,760   8,775  -0.17%  10.19%\par Thailand\tab \tab \tab 37.48   37.50  -0.05%   3.82%\par Philippines\tab \tab    38.90   38.95  -0.13%   1.43%\par Taiwan\tab \tab \tab   33.05   33.10  -0.15%   2.96%\par South Korea\tab \tab    1,223   1,216   0.58%   3.21%\par India\tab \tab \tab    42.54   42.50   0.09%   0.12%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((James Saft, London newsroom +171 542 2734)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 