\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2 -2: Seen Entering Mkt Twice \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1999\par 15:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early Thursday, as the real (BRR) continued to trade weaker than BRR2.00, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to confirm any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday and Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it had stepped into the market - its first \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it free-floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-January. \par \par \uc2  But traders in Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro said they saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  enter the market at least twice Thursday - first selling around $50 million and then going into the market for a second time around 1420 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The real opened at BRR2.03 to the dollar and was trading at BRR2.04 at 1430 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is expensive and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  knows it, so they're monitoring the situation very closely," said one Sao Paulo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  "(The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) wants to keep the real at about its current level, but the market remains under a lot of pressure," he added. "It could easily move to above BRR2.10/dlr." \par \par \uc2  The real has come under renewed pressure this week mainly because of future contract expirations Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-02-99 \par \par \uc2  1439GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2p01i18\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
