\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's International Reserves Slip To $35.71 Billion \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1999\par 21:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO -(Dow Jones)- Brazil's international reserves fell to $35.71 billion Wednesday from $35.74 billion the previous day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has announced reserves daily since Feb. 1. Prior to that, reserves figures were announced monthly, with as much as a three-week lag in the information. \par \par \uc2  The current reserves figure includes $9.4 billion made available to Brazil in December as part of a $41.5 billion aid package coordinated by the International Monetary Fund. Brazil is expected to draw down a second allotment in international funding of about $9 billion before the end of March. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's reserves don't account for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Tuesday. A bank spokesman said Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be built in to Thursday's reserve levels, which will be announced with a one day lag, which would be Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is recorded in the numbers of two days later," the spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's current reserves figure is down from $44.56 billion at the end of 1998 and more than $70 billion last July. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329dv2p01yv2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
