\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil forex interventions \highlight\uc2  risky. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Gill Tudor \par \uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1999\par 18:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two days could create a dangerous target level for speculators to attack, analysts said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to sell dollars on Tuesday for the first time since the embattled real was floated just over a month ago, hauling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to around 2.0 to the dollar after it slid to 2.07. \par \par \uc2  A second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday held the real at a similar level after it slipped to 2.02, surprising some analysts who had seen the previous day's move as a one-off. \par \par \uc2  "I'm not very positive about it," said Jerome Booth, head of research at ANZ Investment Bank in London. "If there's any hint of big support it would be a red rag to a bull - you really will get people having a go at it." \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the real is not currently under serious assault after last month's tumble, but it is under consistent pressure as \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures near their expiry date on Friday and Brazilian firms repay maturing foreign debts which cannot be rolled over. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slid around 40 percent against the dollar since mid-January, when Brazil adjusted and then abandoned a tight \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime that had snuffed out hyperinflation. \par \par \uc2  The devaluation, which threatened to throw wider emerging markets into fresh turmoil, has revived inflation fears and forced up interest rates, deepening \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recession. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to be aimed at ironing out sharp daily \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts in thin liquidity. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman said on Wednesday the bank "may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary and in a limited way to contain unruly movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would want to avoid giving any sign that it was defending a set exchange rate, for fear of sparking the very speculative attack it sought to head off. \par \par \uc2  But the market could start reading an implicit defence level into the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added, raising the spectre of a renewed onslaught on the real. \par \par \uc2  "I still don't think they want to give the market the impression they're defending any particular level, although two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  around this 2.0 level do seem to be trying to establish some sort of temporary psychological barrier," said Peter West, chief economist at BBV Securities in London. \par \par \uc2  "The danger of doing that is you set up a target for the markets to shoot down." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to mount a strong defence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in such circumstances, as it would want to avoid haemorrhaging foreign reserves in an ultimately futile battle against the market. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said Tuesday's move may already have sent the wrong signal. \par \par \uc2  "Unfortunately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have drawn a line in the sand at around two to the dollar, which we think is quite dangerous," said Jake Moore, emerging markets strategist at Barclay's Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  But others said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gamble could pay off provided some kind of good news came swiftly to soothe investors' nerves. \par \par \uc2  That could be in the shape of a revised agreement with the International Monetary Fund, or the confirmation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's president-in-waiting, Arminio Fraga. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said on Wednesday it hoped to finalise a post-devaluation deal this week that would allow payments to resume under a $41.5 billion rescue package drawn up last year. \par \par \uc2  The Senate's confirmation hearing for Fraga, a former aide to billionaire financier George Soros, has been set for Friday. ((London Newsroom +44 171 542 6414, fax 583 7239, gill.tudor@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2o03x9a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
